xecutes both ./bin/du and gdu with\n    36→      the same arguments, environment, and working directory.\n    37→  - id: F5\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    40→      produce identical size values and path listings because they stat the same files on\n    41→      the same filesystem.\n    42→  - id: F6\n    43→    step: |\n    44→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    45→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    46→\n    47→touchpoints:\n    48→  - T1: \"cmd/du — recursive traversal, block accumulation, hard-link dedup, flag modes (prd009-du R1, R2, R3, R4, R5)\"\n    49→  - T2: \"pkg/sys — Stat/Lstat for st_blocks, st_dev, st_ino, InstallSIGPIPEHandler\"\n    50→  - T3: \"pkg/format — HumanSize for -h output\"\n    51→  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n    52→\n    53→success_criteria:\n    54→  - id: S1\n    55→    criterion: cmd/du compiles and ./bin/du exists after mage build.\n    56→  - id: S2\n    57→    criterion: |\n    58→      Default recursive mode produces one line per subdirectory and the root directory,\n    59→      matching gdu -k output on the same fixture.\n    60→  - id: S3\n    61→    criterion: |\n    62→      -s summary mode produces one line per argument with the total size, matching gdu -sk\n    63→      output.\n    64→  - id: S4\n    65→    criterion: |\n    66→      -a all-files mode produces one line per file and directory, matching gdu -ak output.\n    67→  - id: S5\n    68→    criterion: |\n    69→      -h human-readable mode produces size strings (K/M/G) that match gdu -h output on the\n    70→      same fixture.\n    71→  - id: S6\n    72→    criterion: |\n    73→      -c grand total mode produces a \"total\" line after all arguments, matching gdu -ck output.\n    74→  - id: S7\n    75→    criterion: |\n    76→      Hard-link deduplication works: a fixture with two directory entries pointing to the same\n    77→      inode produces a total that counts the file's blocks only once, matching gdu behavior.\n    78→  - id: S8\n    79→    criterion: |\n    80→      --apparent-size mode uses st_size instead of st_blocks, matching gdu --apparent-size\n    81→      output.\n    82→  - id: S9\n    83→    criterion: |\n    84→      The differential test passes for all flag combinations: default -k, -sk, -ak, -h,\n    85→      -ck, -d 1, --apparent-size, and missing path.\n    86→\n    87→out_of_scope:\n    88→  - Cross-filesystem behavior (files on different mount points) is not tested in the\n    89→    differential harness; both binaries see the same single filesystem.\n    90→  - SIGPIPE handling is specified in prd009-du R5.1 but is not directly testable in the\n    91→    differential harness.\n    92→  - Sparse file creation depends on the filesystem; --apparent-size tests use a regular file\n    93→    with known size rather than a true sparse file.\n    94→\n    95→test_suite: test-rel01.3\n    96→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019JcFbbPL1FESob2s9FR1Yr","session_id":"06a6dad7-588e-4321-87aa-0af726b7dedc","uuid":"faab41f3-3ebe-458d-861c-dd11810d6c8f"}
