— Stat/Lstat for st_blocks, st_dev, st_ino, InstallSIGPIPEHandler\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/format — HumanSize for -h output\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/du compiles and ./bin/du exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      Default recursive mode produces one line per subdirectory and the root directory,\n      matching gdu -k output on the same fixture.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      -s summary mode produces one line per argument with the total size, matching gdu -sk\n      output.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      -a all-files mode produces one line per file and directory, matching gdu -ak output.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      -h human-readable mode produces size strings (K/M/G) that match gdu -h output on the\n      same fixture.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      -c grand total mode produces a \"total\" line after all arguments, matching gdu -ck output.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      Hard-link deduplication works: a fixture with two directory entries pointing to the same\n      inode produces a total that counts the file's blocks only once, matching gdu behavior.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: |\n      --apparent-size mode uses st_size instead of st_blocks, matching gdu --apparent-size\n      output.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for all flag combinations: default -k, -sk, -ak, -h,\n      -ck, -d 1, --apparent-size, and missing path.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Cross-filesystem behavior (files on different mount points) is not tested in the\n    differential harness; both binaries see the same single filesystem.\n  - SIGPIPE handling is specified in prd009-du R5.1 but is not directly testable in the\n    differential harness.\n  - Sparse file creation depends on the filesystem; --apparent-size tests use a regular file\n    with known size rather than a true sparse file.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel01.3\n```\n\